u need to read relevant history do a  background check  investigate policies suggested and also  look into opposing views  why might there be critics is the  criticism legitimate  is the critic qualified eventually by  gathering all that information  you will be able to form a more sound  understanding of the concept in question  reading about specific topics is not  really enough  in order to understand the topic deeply  you need to test it and re-evaluate it  based on scrutiny and skepticism learn  to discuss the topic with other fellow  thinkers  online and offline in order to form a  solid and confident view  understand the implication of your  choice and realize whether or not  it is affected by personal biases  emotions and  outside manipulative views that's why i  constantly stress out the importance of  self-awareness  we live in a time where people are  constantly fighting for our attention  and they will say anything to win it a  self-aware critical thinker needs to  battle his own  float perception and deeply scrutinize  his or her personal issues  in order to be capable of forming a  reasoned and clear view on a topic  critical thinking is rational thinking  that involves critique  what this means is that you need to be  able to think rationally based on  information collected by your  environment  but at the same time question your own  judgment meaning  avoid limiting beliefs and biases in  order to form the most ideal version of  truth possible  truth is quite precious especially in a  time where truth is being manipulated  and concealed for personal gain  during such times critical thinking  gives a bit of control over truth  and the ability to be constantly ready  for the things to come  never stop cultivating it  hey guys this video is sponsored by  datacamp  datacamp is an amazing online platform  that makes it easy to build data  analytical skills at your own pace  with great interactive courses i'm  really proud actually of this  sponsorship because  datacamp is a platform i have used in  the past and it really helped me improve  my skills in programming languages like  sql and python  i have studied electrical engineering  and business so  learning to analyze and manipulate data  was a huge part of my studies and work  anybody who is in the specific domain  will find data camps course is simply  incredible  but even if you're not part of the  technology sector  experimenting and immersing yourself in  this kind of programming can help you  think better  data analysis requires a very structured  way of thinking  and it also helps you develop advanced  analytical skills  as a thinker and a writer i realized  that my involvement in programming  and data analysis has helped me  enormously it has helped me  think creatively properly evaluate the  way i write  and also optimize the structure of my  thinking processes  any person who considers him or herself  a critical thinker  can benefit immensely from such practice  so  you know data can be the best place to  start  if you want to get started use the link  in the description below  and check out the first chapter of any  data cam course  you like for free thanks for watching  see you soon adrian out


